# Capability Capsules  -  v2

A **Capability Capsule (CC)** is a versioned software package with **capabilities**, **applications**, or both. A capability is one callable action. An application is software the runner starts and manages, such as an inference engine or test service. A sealed release fixes package bytes; a call returns outputs and a receipt; starting an application returns an instance with endpoints and lifecycle state.

The Factory can produce the engine, its coding/profiling tools and its test environment using this package model. The engine payload need not implement the CC tool protocol. Packaging it as a CC provides a common preparation, authorization, identity and lifecycle boundary.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    author["Author / brief"] --> declaration["Declaration or request"]
    declaration --> factory["Software Factory"]
    factory --> source["Exact repository + patch + dependencies"]
    source --> build["Materialize / build"]
    build --> release["Immutable CC release: native payload or pinned image"]
    release --> catalog["Optional catalog"]
    catalog --> agent["Lab agent"]
    agent --> runner["Runner: prepare and authorize"]
    release --> runner
    runner -->|"call capability"| tool["Outputs + receipt"]
    runner -->|"start application"| instance["Instance + endpoints + logs"]
    instance --> measurement["Measurement capability"]
    measurement --> tool
    tool -. identifies .-> release
    instance -. identifies .-> release
    release -. lineage .-> build
    build -. materials .-> source
    tool --> evaluator["Independent evaluation when requested"]
```

The host owns identity, grants, budgets, resource handles and receipts. Native coding sessions, worktrees and subagent delegation remain native; ordinary internal tools do not each need a capsule.

